Subject: [PATCH 14/98] feat(cli-runner): add 3-layer context overflow
 protection (#13)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* feat(cli-runner): add 3-layer context overflow protection

Layer 1 - Pre-flight guard: estimate tokens after building system prompt,
downgrade bootstrap profile (normal → reduced → minimal) if exceeding
70% of context window.

Layer 2 - Overflow retry: on context overflow error, rebuild with minimal
bootstrap and retry once. Second failure gives explicit error suggesting
pi-embedded runtime or task splitting.

Layer 3 - Dynamic budget: resolveBootstrapBudgetForModel() calculates
bootstrap char budget from model context window (reserve 30%, min 30K tokens).

Adds BootstrapProfile type with normal/reduced/minimal configs,
observability logging (estimated_tokens, context_window, reserve,
trim_profile, retry_count), and 14 unit tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(cli-runner): connect Layer 3 dynamic budget + include task prompt in guard

P0-1: resolveBootstrapTotalMaxChars() now receives contextWindowTokens
so the dynamic budget actually affects the initial bootstrap build.

P0-2: Pre-flight token estimation now includes promptForRun (user task
prompt + prepended context), not just the system prompt. Prevents the
guard from passing when the total prompt would still overflow.

Context window resolution moved earlier (before bootstrap build) so it
serves both Layer 3 (initial budget) and Layer 1 (pre-flight guard).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(cli-runner): wire Layer 3 dynamic budget into actual file injection

resolveBootstrapContextForRun() now accepts contextWindowTokens and
passes it to resolveBootstrapTotalMaxChars(), so the dynamic budget
controls the actual bootstrap file injection—not just the analysis/report.

Previously contextWindowTokens only affected the stats layer while
buildBootstrapContextFiles() still used the static 150K default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

